{"term":"stumble","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4251ec62d146deab6c","definition":"A fall, trip or substantial misstep.","example":"I went to his aid. As he said, a board in the floor was loose. His stepping on it unawares had caused his stumble.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stumble#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:39be8406415960a5bf","definition":"An error or blunder.","example":"Possibly Mr. Carrados was considering it from his own way round for he did not appear to notice anything in her stumble.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["blooper","blunder","boo-boo","defect","error","fault","faux pas","fluff","gaffe","lapse","mistake","slip","thinko"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stumble#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cc569a786c36421e13","definition":"A clumsy walk.","example":"From the ground, Colombo’s port does not look like much. Those entering it are greeted by wire fences, walls dating back to colonial times and security posts. For mariners leaving the port after lonely nights on the high seas, the delights of the B52 Night Club and Stallion Pub lie a stumble away.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stumble#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:490a8e74ce8fe6f2c3","definition":"To misstep; to walk or run clumsily; to trip or fall.","example":"He stumbled over a rock.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["stumble across","stumble against","stumblebum","stumble-drunk","stumble into","stumble on","stumble onto","stumbler","stumblesome","stumble upon","stumbly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stumble#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1e02b352b6ab3fb77b","definition":"To make mistakes, to have trouble.","example":"I always stumble over verbs in Spanish.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["blunder","err"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["stumble across","stumble against","stumblebum","stumble-drunk","stumble into","stumble on","stumble onto","stumbler","stumblesome","stumble upon","stumbly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stumble#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:38bbc8eb6f48b8b315","definition":"To cause to stumble or trip.","example":"Slowly, I turned around and the shock of it stumbled me back a few steps.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["trip up"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["stumble across","stumble against","stumblebum","stumble-drunk","stumble into","stumble on","stumble onto","stumbler","stumblesome","stumble upon","stumbly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stumble#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7200b98ccd02e30eab","definition":"To mislead, to cause to err or fall.","example":"False and dazzling fires to stumble men.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["confound"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["stumble across","stumble against","stumblebum","stumble-drunk","stumble into","stumble on","stumble onto","stumbler","stumblesome","stumble upon","stumbly"],"sour